  "scope": "Error-report entry coordination and retry/terminal proposal assembly move to the product adapter; live lease admission, authoritative journal commit, terminal publication and group visibility retain native owners.",
  "limitations": [
    "Trusted product policy, not raw ingress or the standalone generic VM. Input bounds, provenance, reporting authority and trusted time remain caller obligations; a retry plan is not dispatch authority.",
    "Callbacks run once without coordinator retry or rollback. Journal transactions retain their original rollback boundaries. Visibility may fail after commit, and its fault remains a terminal observation.",
    "The frozen entry shares the existing retry planner, metadata validators, state machinery and journals; it proves coordinator compatibility rather than independent implementation of those lower layers.",
    "Native result conversion/settlement, dispatch-claim coordination, journal ownership, complete host-neutral durable recovery, vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. Native completion and maturity are unchanged.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no Linux, GUI or remote CI run. The existing 280-file standalone checkpoint was integrity-checked, not freshly exported or retested."
  ],
